# Review: GitHub two-way file sync

This spec describes a future design, and almost none of it is built. plugin-github has no `file-sync/`
directory and no `GitHubCapabilities.FileMapping` (its capabilities file declares only `LinkSource`); no
`SyncGitHubFiles` op, `FileMarker`, `VersionLink` or `TextMerge` helper exists; and `github-api.ts` has
none of the git reads and writes (`fetchBranchHead`, `compareCommits`, `fetchTree`, `fetchBlob`,
`commitFiles`, `ensurePullRequest`). Searched plugin-github and plugin-code `src/` for each name.

The only existing pieces are on the plugin-code side, and they do not match the contract. `Spec.content` is a
`Ref<Text>`, as F-6.2 needs. `CodeOperation.ImportSpec` exists under the spec's key, but it links a `.mdl`
file in a local checkout by a `github:` source key and reads it from the file system; it takes neither
`FileImportInput` nor returns heads. There is no `ExportSpec`. Automerge's `changeAt` is available on the
ECHO object core (`object-core.ts`), which answers open question 1, but nothing wraps it for `Text`.

Of 38 items: 0 done, 0 untested, 1 partial, 1 diverged, 36 missing.

